# FFmpeg 9.0.2 configure flags for the Coach Core film validator (FILM-S2a).
# One flag per line; '#' starts a comment. Mirrors the LGPL-only minimal recipe
# in docs/security/FOUNDER_DECISION_PACKET.md §5, plus three additions marked
# [S2a]: --disable-debug and strip (smaller, reproducible), --extra-ldflags=-static
# (self-contained binary), -ffile-prefix-map (reproducible paths), and the
# `null` muxer (libavformat/nullenc.c, LGPL) so the validator can run a full
# decode check with `-f null -` without writing any output file.
# configure itself auto-selects these LGPL core filters for the ffmpeg tool:
# aformat anull atrim crop format hflip null rotate transpose trim vflip.
# Deliberately ABSENT: --enable-gpl, --enable-version3, --enable-nonfree, any
# external library (libx264/libx265/...). Adding any of these changes the
# licence of the result and must go through review.
--disable-everything
--disable-autodetect
--disable-network
--disable-doc
--disable-ffplay
--enable-ffmpeg
--enable-ffprobe
--enable-protocol=file
--enable-demuxer=mov
--enable-muxer=mp4,image2,null
--enable-decoder=h264,aac
--enable-encoder=mjpeg
--enable-parser=h264,aac
--enable-bsf=h264_mp4toannexb
--enable-swscale
--enable-filter=scale,crop,format
--enable-static
--disable-shared
--enable-small
--disable-debug
--extra-ldflags=-static
--pkg-config-flags=--static
